From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a property of a window that is gone does not end the process

When a request to set, delete or read a property of an X window failed
with BadWindow -- the window destroyed meanwhile, by another thread or
another program -- the error went to Xlib's own handler, which ends the
process. The shell, explorer, ended so on David's X1 when touches came
quickly (2026-10-04: "X Error of failed request: BadWindow, Major opcode
18 (X_ChangeProperty)"; sg-session started it again). Such errors are now
ignored, as Wine already ignores BadWindow on focus, configure and
send-event requests, and the first ones are reported with the window's
id, so where they come from can be found.

Test: test/xpropgone-gate.sh with test/xpropgone-probe.c and
test/xpropgone-destroy.c (mutant SG_MUTANT_X_PROP_FATAL).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
@@ -205,6 +205,24 @@
         (event->error_code == BadMatch ||
          event->error_code == BadWindow)) return TRUE;
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_X_PROP_FATAL
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a property set, deleted or read on a window that is
+     * gone meanwhile (another thread or program destroyed it) is no reason to
+     * end the process -- Xlib's handler ended the shell, explorer, when
+     * touches came quickly on David's X1 (2026-10-04: BadWindow on
+     * X_ChangeProperty). Said, so the window can be found. */
+    if ((event->request_code == X_ChangeProperty ||
+         event->request_code == X_DeleteProperty ||
+         event->request_code == X_GetProperty) &&
+        event->error_code == BadWindow)
+    {
+        static LONG said;
+        if (InterlockedIncrement( &said ) <= 20)
+            ERR( "window %lx gone: request %u (property) ignored\n", event->resourceid, event->request_code );
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* the clipboard display interacts with external windows, ignore all errors */
     if (display == clipboard_display) return TRUE;
 
